      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve the test by splitting the monolithic test into focused, well-named test methods, improving variable names, and moving the `@SuppressWarnings` to only where needed.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test splits the original monolithic `testStdMethods` into six focused, descriptively-named test methods (`testToString`, `testHashCodeIsNonZero`, `testEqualsReflexivity`, `testEqualsReturnsFalseForNull`, `testEqualsReturnsFalseForDifferentType`, `testEqualsReturnsTrueForValuesWithIdenticalFields`, and `testEqualsReturnsFalseWhenFieldsDiffer`), moves `@SuppressWarnings` to only the methods that need it, and renames variables like `equals1`/`equals2` to `base`/`equals1`/`equals2` for clarity — all while preserving the exact same method calls and assertions."
